load("@rules_kubectl//kubectl:defs.bzl", "kubectl_toolchain") kubectl_toolchain(name, kubectl, version) A kubectl toolchain. Rules consume it through @rules_kubectl//kubectl:toolchain_type: def _impl(ctx): toolchain = ctx.toolchains["@rules_kubectl//kubectl:toolchain_type"] ctx.actions.run( executable = toolchain.kubectl, ... ) The ToolchainInfo carries kubectl (the binary File) and version (a string, possibly empty). @rules_kubectl//kubectl:current_toolchain exposes the binary through two make variables: KUBECTL is its execpath, for use in actions, and KUBECTL_RLOCATIONPATH is its rlocationpath, for looking it up in runfiles. genrule( name = "pods", outs = ["pods.txt"], cmd = "$(KUBECTL) version --client > $@", toolchains = ["@rules_kubectl//kubectl:current_toolchain"],
) sh_test( name = "pods_test", srcs = ["pods_test.sh"], data = ["@rules_kubectl//kubectl:current_toolchain"], env = {"KUBECTL": "$(KUBECTL_RLOCATIONPATH)"}, toolchains = ["@rules_kubectl//kubectl:current_toolchain"],
) ATTRIBUTES Name Description Type Mandatory Default name A unique name for this target. Name required kubectl A kubectl binary. Label required version The version of kubectl, without a leading v. Informational. String optional ""

