load("@rules_kubectl//kubectl:defs.bzl", "kubectl_binary") kubectl_binary(name, args, data, env, kubectl, **kwargs) An executable that runs kubectl with a fixed set of arguments. The target is meant for bazel run. Anything passed after -- is appended to args, and kubectl starts in the directory bazel run was invoked from, so relative paths on the command line resolve the way they would for a locally installed kubectl. Files Bazel knows about are referenced with $(rlocationpath <label>) in args and env. The launcher resolves them through runfiles at run time, which means the executable also works when another binary or test runs it. load("@rules_kubectl//kubectl:defs.bzl", "kubectl_binary") kubectl_binary( name = "apply", args = [ "apply", "--filename=$(rlocationpath :manifests)", ], data = [":manifests"],
) kubectl_binary( name = "staging_pods", args = ["get", "pods"], data = ["staging.kubeconfig"], env = {"KUBECONFIG": "$(rlocationpath staging.kubeconfig)"},
) bazel run //deploy:apply -- --namespace my-namespace Nothing about clusters, contexts or namespaces is decided here; that is left to the arguments and the environment. PARAMETERS Name Description Default Value name The name of the target. none args Arguments for kubectl. $(rlocationpath <label>) references files from data. [] data Files kubectl may read at run time. [] env Environment variables set for kubectl, overriding inherited values. $(rlocationpath <label>) references files from data. {} kubectl A specific kubectl binary. By default the binary of the resolved toolchain is used. None kwargs Additional keyword arguments for the underlying go_binary, such as visibility. none

